{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1142560-c20-changeling-kingdoms-in-the-pacific-northwest-of-the-u-s-a","id":1142560,"title":"C20 Changeling Kingdoms in the Pacific Northwest of the U.S.A.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-21T09:25:51-07:00","id":1142560,"title":"C20 Changeling Kingdoms in the Pacific Northwest of the U.S.A.","content":"I enjoyed Changeling back when it came out and I'm planning on adding some Changeling elements to a Portland-based Mage campaign.<br /> <br /> Is there any information on Changeling kingdoms in the Pacific Northwest of the U.S.A., around Portland, Oregon?<br /> <br /> If so, I'd appreciate it if someone could summarize as my cash flow is insufficient to acquire C20 at present.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T10:02:16-07:00","id":1142576,"title":"","content":"I'm planning in doing a game in Seattle, so I did some research about it. Unhappily the books gave not much information.<br /> <br /> All the Pacific United States is one kingdom, Kingdom of Pacifica. It takes Washington, Oregon and California. All Inside is divided in Duchies. Those are more plentiful (and well explained) in the California State, and very much just brushed out on the other states.<br /> <br /> This website basically sums up all that is known (and create a few things): <a href=\"http://wodcityofangels.com/page.php?109.6\" target=\"_blank\">http://wodcityofangels.com/page.php?109.6</a>, even with maps, so it is your best source to learn what you want and build upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T12:03:24-07:00","id":1142640,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the information-the map list is for Los Angeles but gives me some ideas on where to put things in Portland once I get some maps. Sounds like I just go with my gut and story needs given the lacunas in information.<br /> <br /> Good luck on your game in Seattle! We did some activity there in a GURPS Mage game where one character was a trickster, maybe even a pooka. The Space Needle we kept calling the Space Noodle because one of the players called it that. I made the Space Noodle, er Space Needle a Void Engineer Construct, so that the pooka got to prank them. . .<br /> <br /> You'll definitely want to think of Seattle's music scene and Quintar Taylor's <i>The Forging of a Black Community</i> was an illuminating history of African-Americans in Seattle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T19:29:27-07:00","id":1142784,"title":"","content":"For better or for worse, the only Kingdom really fleshed out was Willows. To me the benefit of having an official game source for a geographic location is to save time when running your own game. It's a lot of work to create a city setting! But if you have the time you can really personalize the setting more by doing it yourself, especially if you really know the area. Even if you've never been to a place we're in the wonderful Internet age where you can easily look up what you need. I've created several historical and modern settings for Changeling without ever having been to that location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T22:57:54-07:00","id":1142815,"title":"","content":"When using a game setting, I like to see the take on the geography and how things fit in, even if I make my own tweaks. So, one of my favorite settings is the Kingdoms of Kalamar setting, which is primarily for D&amp;D. It has that level of detail where you can start to see potential drama, has great maps and great plot hooks and while full of interesting NPCs, makes the player characters the protagonists of the story.<br /> <br /> I attended college in Portland many years ago, so I've been there and will be using the internet to fill out some of the areas I don't know and that have changed since then. One decision I made is that all factions consider Powell's City of Books to be 'sacred ground' and neutral. A bookstore that fills three city blocks and which is the largest bookstore west of the Mississippi is filled with Glamour and Quintessence. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T18:51:08-07:00","id":1143375,"title":"","content":"I've been to Portland many times and Powell's is AMAZING! I love that you made that a kind of Elysium for kithain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T21:58:02-07:00","id":1143674,"title":"","content":"Powell's is an asylum for everyone in my Mage game--vampires, mages, werewolves and kithain. No one wants to break the peace, but the PCs may go a different route. I have the Glass Walkers holding it as a cairn, about a level 2 cairrn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T22:59:23-07:00","id":1144295,"title":"","content":"And rules #2 and #3 of the Mage campaign are:<br /> #2. Powell's is neutral ground (holy ground, Highlander, but the youngest player completely missed the reference).<br /> #3. Do not go into <i>properly</i> signed 'staff only' areas of Powell's lest you be eaten. Essentially, the Glass Walkers will tear up any interlopers. Since lots of different people come through Powell's you got to make sure the signs are right--Glass Walker wards make it pretty clear 'don't go there,' whereas a regular sign might have been put there by anyone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}